{{also|Fett}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gml|vet}}, from {{der|de|osx|*fētid}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*faitid}}. {{doublet|de|feist}}. In the colloquial sense perhaps a {{cal|de|en|phat|nocap=1}} via hip-hop culture.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/fɛt/}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|comp}}

# [[fat]]
#: {{uxi|de|'''Fette''' Menschen sind oft ungesund.|'''Fat''' people are often unhealthy.}}
# {{lb|de|of food}} [[rich]], containing a lot of fat
# {{lb|de|typography}} [[bold]]
#: {{uxi|de|In diesem Satz ist nur das Wort „'''fett'''“ '''fett''' geschrieben.|In this sentence, only the word “'''bold'''” is written in '''bold'''.}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} [[awesome]], [[phat]]
#: {{uxi|de|Das war echt '''fett'''.|This was really '''awesome'''.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Sie hat 'nen '''fetten''' Vertrag an Land gezogen.|She got a very '''profitable''' contract.}}
# {{lb|de|Austria|colloquial}} [[drunk]]
#: {{syn|de|besoffen|betrunken|blau|dicht}}

